"use strict";
const adventure17={slug:"the-tumbleweed-has-right-of-way",title:"The Tumbleweed Has Right of Way",subtitle:"One giant tumbleweed enters traffic and Tucson quietly gives it driving privileges.",scenes:[{title:"Dead Bush Crossing",body:`<p>You are driving home when a tumbleweed the size of a refrigerator rolls into your lane.</p><p>You stop. It stops.</p><p>The driver behind you honks.</p><p>The tumbleweed refuses to be intimidated.</p>`,question:"What do you do?",choices:[["A","Wait for it to cross.","You wait. It waits. You are now in a standoff with a dead bush."],["B","Drive slowly around it.","The tumbleweed changes direction too. You are being defended by vegetation."],["C","Give it a little honk.","Nothing. Apparently tumbleweeds do not respond to criticism."],["D","Let it hit the car.","THUMP. It bounces off your bumper and keeps going. Tucson's cheapest hit-and-run."]],next:1},{title:"It Brought Friends",body:`<p>You continue driving.</p><p>Another tumbleweed rolls into the road. Then another.</p><p>Three of them are now moving together while traffic follows at a respectful distance.</p><p>Nobody remembers agreeing to this.</p>`,question:"What now?",choices:[["A","Follow them.","They turn left. You turn left. Your navigation app says RECALCULATING, then seems to give up."],["B","Try to pass.","One rolls toward your lane. You retreat. The tumbleweeds have invented defensive driving."],["C","Take a picture while safely stopped.","The photo makes them look tiny. Nobody will believe you were delayed by shrubbery."],["D","Treat them like pedestrians.","You stop and wave them across. The driver behind you does the same. A traffic rule is born without paperwork."]],next:2},{title:"Tumbleweed Traffic Law",body:`<p>At the next intersection, more tumbleweeds arrive.</p><p>Cars stop. The tumbleweeds roll through.</p><p>A police cruiser pulls up. The officer looks at the tumbleweeds, looks at the drivers, and decides not to be the first person in Arizona to argue with twenty bushes.</p>`,question:"Who has the right of way?",choices:[["A","The cars.","Technically convincing. Nobody moves."],["B","The tumbleweeds.","Everyone waits. The tumbleweeds cross with the confidence of people who have excellent lawyers."],["C","Whoever got there first.","Nobody can determine when the tumbleweed arrived. It has no timestamp and refuses questions."],["D","Ask the police officer.","He points toward the tumbleweeds and says, “I'm not touching those.” This becomes the official ruling."]],next:3},{title:"You Learn the Rule",body:`<p>The wind changes and the tumbleweeds finally roll away.</p><p>Traffic starts moving again.</p><p>Two miles later, one lonely tumbleweed approaches a crosswalk.</p><p>You hit the brakes automatically. So does the driver beside you.</p><p>Neither of you is taking chances anymore.</p>`,question:"How does this end?",final:true,choices:[["A","Always yield from now on.","Your insurance company has no category for this.","The Tumbleweed Has Right of Way","Nobody knows whether it is the law. Nobody wants to be the test case."],["B","Install a dashcam.","Your next encounter gets 800,000 views. Half the comments say it is fake.","Tucson Provides Documentation","The other half say, “That's nothing. You should've seen Tuesday.”"],["C","Report it to the city.","A committee begins studying mobile vegetation.","Government Moves Slower Than Tumbleweed","The tumbleweed leaves before the first meeting."],["D","Decide the tumbleweed won.","You reach home. Something scratches against the garage door. There it is.","It Knows Where You Live","Tomorrow you're taking the bus."]] }]};